our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 360+4\\times 420 \\\\  & =720+1\\,680 \\\\  & =2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282932 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282933 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282934 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282935 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282936 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1041 "selection" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282934 13194139534233 true] [17592186282931 1110 #uuid "6b661837-27bb-5ece-a120-0ddf7f7452d6" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282932 1034 "1\\,280\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282932 1111 #uuid "b3916a7c-e231-5f13-bf5c-cacbbbe98ac7" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282933 1034 "1\\,070\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282933 1111 #uuid "cdde5fdf-534d-5e22-a091-af8e8619b61c" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282934 1034 "2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282934 1111 #uuid "0a815c2f-4fb2-5ca0-8b25-3b0628a86930" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282935 1034 "2\\,460\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282935 1111 #uuid "b06d9ab2-63b9-5b32-9328-a36c21399110" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282936 1034 "2\\,160\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282936 1111 #uuid "addaa780-8ea2-511a-8154-9c95664852bf" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282937 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282938 13194139534233 true] [17592186282937 1089 "q-61903" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282937 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534233 true] [17592186282937 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/0c4cf0ae740f876576ff140f488432dbfae9d26eb5e68e9bafbcc9b5a5bb286b.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism above if it is $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $3\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282937 1113 #uuid "5c5c0ab9-8ba3-5d4c-b7d4-04c7169ce9d0" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282937 1145 "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/98eb9b74a15ad1cad75974496a370fb9b9b28f7ff57bc319500fcd31492216d3.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 3=12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $3\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=3\\times 3=9\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the rectangular prism consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 12+2\\times 9 \\\\  & =48+18 \\\\  & =66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282939 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282940 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282941 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282942 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282943 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1041 "selection" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282940 13194139534233 true] [17592186282938 1110 #uuid "5edf2a96-b1f8-5813-bf8d-903850556da7" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282939 1034 "54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282939 1111 #uuid "a5715275-9443-584a-9f88-4595cb23c2b8" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282940 1034 "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282940 1111 #uuid "b5038f42-936a-55b9-9549-abcb1dbbb0d1" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282941 1034 "60\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282941 1111 #uuid "37bcb9ba-da2d-52d7-a0a7-fd46fe972871" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282942 1034 "21\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282942 1111 #uuid "33c4ed64-44dc-52e9-992a-359432c2db69" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282943 1034 "72\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282943 1111 #uuid "d371b68b-a06f-5b1b-ad6c-f8c89e0a9a57" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282944 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282945 13194139534233 true] [17592186282944 1089 "q-62107" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282944 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534233 true] [17592186282944 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/248ccfcbb3de8ab63622cfaf4c823ae1c1734742f5f8c9f14b1dfae0ff79eed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282944 1113 #uuid "17e99f21-4a32-5f31-9b6f-4f7bf7f5a533" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282944 1145 "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282946 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282947 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282948 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282949 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282950 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1041 "selection" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282949 13194139534233 true] [17592186282945 1110 #uuid "3512f341-753f-57c9-b2bb-c7a6c4172580" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282946 1034 "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282946 1111 #uuid "59fe7ec3-2b47-51f2-a6d8-0c3dcdcb1794" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282947 1034 "15\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139534233 true] [17592186282947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534233 true] [17592186282947 1111 #uuid "